                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If there was a neutral thumbs sideways option, that is what I would rate this.\nGiven it is almost always on sale at 90% off and it does what it says it does I will give it a thumbs up.\nThis game is only really worth it when it is on sale. Do not pay full price. It is not worth even a penny more than when it is 90% off. If I had paid more than CAD $0.59 it likely would have gotten the thumbs down.\nIt is a simple runner game, 3 lanes avoid some objects get the collectible objects. It has jump, and interestingly enough a double jump feature, but that's about as innovative or interesting as this game gets.\nIf you like runner games you will get a small amount of enjoyment from this game and might even play it enough to get all the cards, but will likely spend some time idling it because it's just so...simple. Almost feels like an old android port, no settings or pause feature (not that it needs them)\nThe fact that it's built on the Unreal Engine makes this game take up an unusual amount of GPU and Power resources for it's genre and graphics level. It's the type of game you THINK you can just idle and play another to finish the cards when you are done with it, but it's the type that crashes your computer if you do that. So when you have had your fill (which you will before you get all the cards) go watch a movie.",
